# IMP-02 Turn C — UAT TLS termination environment template. NO real secrets in this file.
#
# These variables are ADDITIVE to platform/edge/uat/.env.example (the accepted Turn-A template,
# left unmodified by Turn C) — they are only consulted when TLS mode is deliberately selected.
#
# EDGE_TLS_ENABLED is a PRESENCE flag, not a boolean. HAProxy's config preprocessor tests
# whether a variable is *defined*, never its value's truthiness — empirically verified during
# Turn C Phase 0 that EDGE_TLS_ENABLED=false still selects the TLS branch identically to
# EDGE_TLS_ENABLED=1. To run the UAT-neutral Turn-A HTTP mode, UNSET this variable entirely;
# do not set it to "false", "0", or any other falsy-looking string.
EDGE_TLS_ENABLED=1

# Path to a PEM file containing BOTH the leaf certificate and its private key concatenated
# (HAProxy's `bind ... ssl crt <path>` convention) — REQUIRED whenever EDGE_TLS_ENABLED is
# defined; startup fails closed with no silent plaintext fallback if this is absent. Generated
# by ./make-certs.sh into ./generated/ (git-ignored) — see README.md.
EDGE_TLS_CRT_PATH=./generated/valid-combined.pem
